# Stable retrieval keys over drifting author spellings.
# This repo's thesis applied to its own history: a name is a filing key,
# not a fingerprint. One person, one canonical identity for attribution,
# regardless of how the committer string drifted at write time.
#
# Without this, `git log --author=Auran` silently drops a fifth of Auran's
# commits (lowercase `auran-theclearing` is a case-sensitive name miss),
# which is worse than failing loudly. See PR #27 §4 and discussion w/ Venice.

Auran <auran@auran.llc> <auran@auran.llc>
Auran <auran@auran.llc> auran-theclearing <auran@auran.llc>
Auran <auran@auran.llc> Auran Andrew <auran@theclear.ing>
